---
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro";
import Navbar from "@components/Navbar.astro";
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import "@styles/global.css";
import "@styles/tokens.css";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Nimbus"
  description="How Nimbus collects, uses, and protects your information."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">
        <svg
          width="14"
          height="14"
          viewBox="0 0 16 16"
          fill="none"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            d="M10 3L5 8l5 5"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        </svg>
        Back to Nimbus
      </a>

      <article class="legal-article">
        <header class="legal-header">
          <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
          <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="legal-date">Last updated: 4 April 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal-body">
          <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
          <p>
            Nimbus is a WordPress plugin for cloud media offloading. We are an
            independent software product reachable at <a
              href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a
            >. When this policy says "Nimbus", "we", "us", or "our" it refers to
            the operator of the Nimbus plugin and the website usenimbus.dev.
          </p>

          <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
          <p>We collect only what is necessary to operate the product:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Purchase information.</strong> When you buy a license, our payment
              processor collects your email address and payment details. We receive
              your email address and the tier of license purchased. We do not store
              full card numbers.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>License validation.</strong> When the plugin is active on a
              WordPress site, it periodically sends your license key and the WordPress
              installation's site URL to our license API (<code
                >api.usenimbus.dev</code
              >) to verify that the license is valid. No data about your site
              visitors is transmitted.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Website logs.</strong> Our web server temporarily records standard
              HTTP logs (IP address, browser, page requested, timestamp). These are
              used for debugging and security and are not retained beyond 30 days.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>To issue and validate your software license.</li>
            <li>
              To contact you about significant product updates or security
              notices (not marketing without consent).
            </li>
            <li>To maintain the security and integrity of our services.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. Data sharing</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data. We may share data
            only with:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Razorpay</strong> (razorpay.com) to process your payment securely.
              Razorpay's privacy policy governs their use of your payment data.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Infrastructure providers</strong> for hosting the license API.
              These operate under data processing agreements.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We have no advertising or analytics partners that receive personal
            data.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Cookies and tracking</h2>
          <p>
            The Nimbus website does not use advertising or analytics tracking
            cookies. Your browser may store a functional session cookie if you
            visit a page that requires authentication, but this is not used for
            cross-site tracking.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Data security</h2>
          <p>
            All data transmitted between the plugin and our license API uses TLS
            (HTTPS) encryption. License keys are stored using secure hashing
            practices. We apply security best-practices to our infrastructure,
            but no system is 100% immune to all threats.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
          <p>
            Your email address and license record are retained for as long as
            your license is active plus a short period after for dispute
            resolution. You may request deletion at any time (see Your Rights
            below). Server log data is purged automatically after 30 days.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to access,
            correct, delete, or export the personal data we hold about you. To
            exercise any of these rights, email us at <a
              href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a
            > and we will respond within 30 days.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Nimbus is a developer tool and is not directed at children under the
            age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy to reflect changes in our practices or for
            legal reasons. When we do, we will update the "last updated" date at
            the top of this page. Material changes will be communicated via
            email to active license holders.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about this policy? Email <a
              href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 7rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    transition: color var(--nmb-t);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--nmb-text);
  }

  /* ── Article ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-article {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--nmb-border-light);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--nmb-text);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-date {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-subtle);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Body typography ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--nmb-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.625rem;
  }

  .legal-body p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 0.875rem;
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.875rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal-body li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--nmb-text-2);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-body code {
    font-family: var(--nmb-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--nmb-accent);
    background: var(--nmb-accent-dim);
    padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
    border-radius: var(--nmb-radius-xs);
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--nmb-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .legal-body a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
